      {
        "id": 227327,
        "name": "gossamerica2",
        "username": "gossamerica2",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/51bf81/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-07-08T21:36:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"rickjonzz\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rickjonzz/48/1934_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> rickjonzz:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m a lazy completionist (and, frankly, not good enough at the game to hit the unlock conditions for some) and have been just waiting for the characters to be unlockable, but when I try, Guise says something like “Think of the Children” and doesn’t unlock. Should I just be more patient and wait or am I going to have to dust off some guides and try to get him the old-fashioned way?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I thought I wasn’t good enough to hit some of the unlock conditions.  But with help from some guides, I pulled them all off, most of them on the first attempt.  And I learned a lot in the process, helping me become a better player (especially against some of the harder villains).  It also gave me something to shoot for rather than just a random game setup.   I think it’s well worth it!</p>",
